The stream appears placid enough, but appearances can be deceiving.	這條溪流看似平靜無波，但外表可能會騙人。
This natural rock bridge connects the Daventry mainland to a small island.	這座天然石橋將戴凡確王國的本土與一座小島連接起來。
This is an old, rickety bridge which seems to be one of the only ways cross the river.	這是一座老舊搖晃的橋，似乎是過河為數不多的方法之一。
How do you use the dagger?	你要怎麼使用短刀？
You don't have the dagger.	你身上沒有短刀。
The troll is bigger than you, stronger than you, and much, MUCH meaner than you.  Better not even try it.	矮精靈比你高大、比你強壯，而且比你兇惡得多，兇惡「非常非常」多。你最好想都別想。
You throw the dagger and it lands in the river, lost for all time.	你把短刀丟出去，短刀落入河中，永遠消失了。
There is no need for that now.	現在沒有必要那麼做。
diamond pouch	鑽石皮袋
gold egg	金蛋
sceptre	王杖
treasure chest	金盒子
gold walnut	金胡桃
Gold Walnut	金胡桃
The troll isn't interested in a plain walnut.	矮精靈對普通的胡桃沒有興趣。
Walnut	胡桃
Why?  To what?	為什麼？要做什麼？
Your skimpy offering doesn't impress the troll.	你這寒酸的供品打動不了矮精靈。
You push the troll as hard as you can.  Unfortunately, the troll doesn't budge an inch.	你使出全力推矮精靈，可惜矮精靈紋風不動。
You certainly cannot do that from here.	你在這裡當然沒辦法這麼做。
The troll turns a very large and pointy deaf ear on your pleas.	矮精靈那對又大又尖的耳朵，對你的懇求充耳不聞。
The troll cannot hear you from there.	矮精靈在那裡聽不見你說話。
TROLL: "Dat's right.  Gimme somethin' valuable and maybe, JUST maybe, I'll letcha cross dis bridge.  If I feel like it.  Which I ain't sure I do."	矮精靈：「沒錯，給我點值錢的東西，也許，『也許』我就讓你過我這座橋。如果我心情好的話。不過我可不確定自己心情好不好。」
You should save your pebbles.  You may need them later.	你該省著點用鵝卵石，之後可能用得到。
You throw a pebble at the troll, but it merely bounces off his thick hide.  He barely notices it.	你朝矮精靈丟了一顆鵝卵石，卻只在他厚厚的皮膚上彈開，他幾乎沒察覺。
You throw the dagger and the troll deftly snatches it out of the air.  What are you going to do now?	你把短刀丟出去，矮精靈靈巧地在半空中把它接住。你現在打算怎麼辦？
You throw the dagger wildly and it sails away, never to be found.	你胡亂把短刀丟出去，短刀飛遠了，再也找不回來。
dagger	短刀
There is no one here to throw the dagger at.	這裡沒有人可以讓你丟短刀。
You do not have the %s.	你身上沒有 %s。
You give the %s to the troll, and it appears to satisfy him.  He tromps off leaving the bridge clear for you to cross.	你把 %s 給了矮精靈，他似乎相當滿意，隨即跺著腳離開，讓出橋來給你通過。
If you want to try that, you should get a little closer.	如果你想試試看，應該再靠近一點。
It's too late now!	現在已經太遲了！
It's too shallow here.	這裡水太淺了。
You need to be in the water to swim.	你得先進到水裡才能游泳。
You need to be in the water to try that.	你得先進到水裡才能嘗試那件事。
The water is not deep enough here for you to dive.	這裡的水不夠深，沒辦法讓你跳水。
The water isn't very deep here.  Diving wouldn't be recommended.	這裡的水不太深，不建議跳水。
The water is very deep here.  Without aid, it is impossible to swim under the water for any length of time.	這裡的水非常深。沒有輔助工具，不可能在水下游太久。
You have nothing to carry the water in.	你身上沒有可以裝水的東西。
Walking in the water seems to have made you visible once again.	走進水裡似乎讓你再次現形了。
This is a well-tended carrot patch.  The carrots look tempting to a hungry traveler.	這是一片照料得很好的胡蘿蔔田，對飢餓的旅人來說，這些胡蘿蔔看起來十分誘人。
A brick border surrounds a well-kept garden.	一圈磚砌的邊界圍繞著一座整理得很好的花園。
You see a brick border surrounding a well-kept garden.	你看見一圈磚砌的邊界，圍繞著一座整理得很好的花園。
There are many large, plump carrots in the garden.	花園裡有許多又大又飽滿的胡蘿蔔。
The carrots are buried in the ground. You must get closer to see them.	胡蘿蔔埋在地裡，你得靠近一點才能看清楚。
You already have a carrot.	你已經有一根胡蘿蔔了。
You're too busy to pick a carrot.	你現在正忙著，沒空摘胡蘿蔔。
You can't pick a carrot while you're invisible.	你隱形的時候沒辦法摘胡蘿蔔。
You must be in the carrot patch to pick a carrot.	你得站在胡蘿蔔田裡才能摘胡蘿蔔。
You pluck a plump, orange carrot from the ground.	你從地裡拔起一根飽滿的橘色胡蘿蔔。
You are standing outside King Edward's castle, which is surrounded by a serpent-filled moat.	你站在愛德華國王的城堡外，城堡四周圍繞著一條滿是巨蛇的護城河。
King Edward the Benevolent, the mighty ruler of Daventry, lives in this castle.	仁慈的愛德華國王，戴凡確王國強大的統治者，就住在這座城堡裡。
You never know what sort of fierce sea creatures lie just beneath the surface of the moat.	你永遠不知道護城河水面下潛伏著什麼樣兇猛的水中生物。
It's your typical moat water: murky and smelly.	這是典型的護城河水：混濁又發臭。
Tendrils of ivy cling to the massive walls of the castle.	藤蔓的卷鬚攀附在城堡厚重的牆上。
It's the king's ivy.  Leave it alone.	那是國王的常春藤，別去碰它。
What!  Are you crazy?	什麼！你瘋了嗎？
But they help to guard the castle! You should let these creatures do their job in peace.	但牠們是在幫忙守衛城堡！你該讓這些生物安心做牠們的工作。
You'd end up inside the serpent.  And what would happen to Daventry then?	你最後會被巨蛇吞進肚子裡。到時戴凡確王國會變成什麼樣子？
Who knows what danger lurks beneath the surface of the murky water.	誰知道混濁的水面下潛伏著什麼樣的危險。
The odor of the murky water is almost unbearable.	這混濁河水的臭味幾乎讓人難以忍受。
You wouldn't want to dive in the serpent-filled moat.	你不會想跳進滿是巨蛇的護城河裡。
The guards do not appreciate people climbing their castle.	衛兵們不喜歡有人爬他們的城堡。
Go ahead.  But it's not recommended.	去吧，不過不建議這麼做。
You'll want to leave those horrible creatures alone.	你最好別去招惹那些可怕的生物。
These serpents would rather eat you than to talk to you.	這些巨蛇寧可吃了你，也不想跟你說話。
You already have water.	你已經有水了。
You don't have a bucket.	你身上沒有水桶。
You fill the bucket with the murky water from the moat.	你用護城河的混濁河水裝滿水桶。
You need to get closer to the water.	你得再靠近水邊一點。
These scaly, slimy serpents cruise the moat searching for unwary trespassers.	這些長滿鱗片、渾身黏滑的巨蛇在護城河中巡遊，尋找不小心闖入的人。
You can see the goat's reflection on the dirty moat water.	你能在骯髒的護城河水面上，看見山羊的倒影。
You can see your reflection on the dirty moat water.	你能在骯髒的護城河水面上，看見自己的倒影。
You've already planted them.	你已經種下它們了。
You ate the beans.	你已經吃掉那些豆子了。
That is not a bad idea, but this is not a very suitable place to plant these beans.  Why don't you try it elsewhere?	這主意不錯，但這裡不太適合種這些豆子，何不去別的地方試試？
You can't plant the beans while you're invisible.	你隱形的時候沒辦法種豆子。
You plant the magical beans in the fertile soil.  Suddenly, something incredible begins to happen!	你把魔豆種進肥沃的土壤裡，突然間，不可思議的事發生了！
You're not in a good place to climb the beanstalk.	你現在的位置不適合爬豆莖。
You are already climbing the beanstalk.	你已經在爬豆莖了。
You must be swimming in order to dive.	你得先游泳，才能潛水。
The current is too strong for diving.	水流太強，沒辦法潛水。
You must be in the water in order to swim.	你得先進到水裡才能游泳。
Although you try to swim, the current is too strong.	你試著游泳，但水流太強了。
The steep embankment prevents you from getting a drink.	陡峭的堤岸讓你沒辦法喝到水。
You're too busy drowning!	你正忙著溺水呢！
The steep embankment prevents you from doing that.	陡峭的堤岸讓你沒辦法這麼做。
The beanstalk's leaves are bigger than you are!	豆莖的葉子比你還大！
Go ahead and climb.	去吧，爬上去。
You are already climbing the beanstalk.  Be careful!	你已經在爬豆莖了，小心點！
They are much too large to carry around.	它們太大了，沒辦法隨身帶著走。
Up here in the clouds, the selection of stones is very poor.	在雲端這裡，能找到的石頭少得可憐。
You are in the Land of the Clouds.  There is a giant here.	你身處雲之國，這裡有一個巨人。
You are in the Land of the Clouds.  It is rumored that a giant lives up here.	你身處雲之國，傳說有個巨人住在這上面。
These gigantic, oddly-shaped trees loom far overhead.	這些形狀怪異的巨樹，高聳在你頭頂遠處。
As you drop through the clouds, your magic ring slips from your finger.	你穿過雲層墜落時，魔戒從你的手指上滑落。
Next time, keep your feet on the ground and your head out of the clouds!	下次記得腳踏實地，別把頭埋進雲裡！
You can hear the chirping of many birds hidden in the trees.	你能聽見許多鳥兒藏在樹裡啁啾鳴叫。
Sir Graham!  Your conduct is unbecoming of a knight.  Fortunately, the birds are flying too fast for you to hit.	格拉漢爵士！你這樣的行為有失騎士風範。幸好那些鳥飛得太快，你打不中牠們。
They're not here right now...but the birds are coming.	牠們現在不在這裡……不過鳥兒正要飛來。
The birds of Daventry are beautiful, are they not?	戴凡確王國的鳥兒很美麗，不是嗎？
You are neither tall enough nor fast enough to do that.	你的身高不夠、速度也不夠快，做不到這件事。
There's no reason to kill the birds in Daventry.   They would never harm you!	沒有理由要殺害戴凡確王國的鳥兒，牠們根本不會傷害你！
The birds of Daventry get up early and catch all the worms they need.	戴凡確王國的鳥兒早起，能抓到牠們需要的所有蟲子。
Your aim could use some improvement.  The dagger flies through the air, and where it lands, you know not where.	你的準頭還有待加強。短刀飛向空中，落在哪裡，你也不知道。
You play a lively, toe-tapping tune on the fiddle.	你用小提琴演奏了一曲輕快、讓人忍不住打拍子的曲子。
The woodcutter and his wife ignore your fiddling. Perhaps they preferred their own music?	樵夫和他的妻子沒理會你的琴聲，也許他們比較喜歡自己的音樂？
Though your fiddle-playing is loud and boisterous, the giant can't hear you above his own snoring.  Good thing, too!	雖然你的琴聲又吵又熱鬧，巨人卻被自己的鼾聲蓋過，根本聽不見。這樣也好！
Obviously, there are no music lovers here.  You put the fiddle away.	這裡顯然沒有愛好音樂的人，你把小提琴收了起來。
You had better practice.  Your aim with the slingshot is poor.	你最好多練習，你用投石器的準頭不太好。
You missed.  Then again, you weren't aiming at anything worthwhile.	你沒打中。不過話說回來，你瞄準的也不是什麼值得打的東西。
Be careful!  There's a sorcerer lurking nearby, just waiting to try out his newest incantation.	小心！附近潛伏著一名巫師，正等著試驗他最新的咒語。
The sorcerer wants to cast his brand-new Paralysis Spell on you.	這名巫師想對你施展他全新的「麻痺咒」。
This sorcerer is a man of few words and many dangerous spells.	這名巫師話不多，卻擁有許多危險的咒語。
Unfortunately, there's nothing in Daventry more dangerous than an angry Sorcerer.  Best to avoid this evil magician than do anything that could cause him to retaliate!	不幸的是，戴凡確王國裡沒有什麼比一名發怒的巫師更危險了。最好避開這名邪惡的法師，別做任何可能招致他報復的事！
Unfortunately, the sorcerer is immune to the magic ring's invisibility spell.	不幸的是，這名巫師不受魔戒隱身咒的影響。
The sorcerer casts his Paralysis Spell, freezing you to the spot.  Satisfied with his deviltry, he departs, leaving you at the mercy of the forest creatures.  Let's hope there are no dangerous creatures skulking about until the spell wears off.	巫師對你施展「麻痺咒」，讓你當場動彈不得。他對自己的惡作劇感到滿意，便揚長而去，留下你任憑森林生物擺布。希望在咒語解除之前，附近沒有危險的生物潛伏。
The powerful spell has counteracted your own magic and removed your invisibility.	這道強大的咒語抵銷了你自己的魔法，讓你的隱身效果消失了。
The Paralysis Spell has worn off.  You're free to move about again, but beware of the Sorcerer's return.	「麻痺咒」的效果已經解除，你又能自由行動了，但要小心巫師回來。
Suddenly you hear the heavy footfalls of an Ogre!  He stomps into the clearing, spots you, and decides to crush the life out of you.	你突然聽見沉重的腳步聲——是一隻鬼怪！他踏著腳步走進空地，一眼看見你，便打定主意要把你活活壓死。
The ogre is itching to take you in his powerful arms and crush your bones!	這隻鬼怪迫不及待想用他強壯的雙臂抓住你，把你的骨頭捏碎！
Talking to this ogre is like talking to a brick wall.  An ANGRY brick wall.	跟這隻鬼怪說話，就像跟一堵牆說話——一堵發怒的牆。
This Ogre is one tough character.  Trying to bring harm to him would be a very bad mistake.  He's got a very thick skin, and a very short temper.	這隻鬼怪是個難纏的角色，想傷害他絕對是天大的錯誤。他皮粗肉厚，脾氣又差。
You don't have anything to try that with.	你身上沒有可以拿來嘗試的東西。
Attempting to bring harm to the ogre will do no good.  He has a very thick skin, and a very short temper.	想傷害這隻鬼怪不會有任何好處，他皮粗肉厚，脾氣又差。
The ogre is confused by your sudden disappearance.  Sneak away now, while you've got the chance!	這隻鬼怪被你突然消失搞得一頭霧水。趁現在有機會，趕緊溜走吧！
Unfortunately, you were too close to the ogre.  He could sense you nearby, despite your invisibility!	不幸的是，你離這隻鬼怪太近了。儘管你隱了形，他還是能察覺你就在附近！
The ogre sees you again!	這隻鬼怪又看見你了！
There is a small dwarf right nearby.  Be careful; this sly little chap is trouble.	附近就有一個矮小的矮人。小心點，這個狡猾的小傢伙是個麻煩人物。
